      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced an overall gross prior year strengthening of GBP 4.162 million in 2024. This was driven by mixed movements across lines of business for accident years up to 2023, with releases in Accident & Health, Property, Casualty, and Property Reinsurance, but a significant strengthening in Liability Reinsurance. The strengthening in Liability Reinsurance is attributed to a revaluation of historic liability reserves in response to increased levels of litigation funding, particularly for years of account 2016 and post. The report also notes that the 2022 account benefited from a modest release from 'old years' and the 2023 account was running better than 2022, but the 2024 account is expected to suffer from recent Los Angeles wildfires and Floridian Hurricanes Helene and Milton. Prior year events like Hurricane Ian (2022) and Maui fires (2023) also impacted earlier periods.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "Change in estimates of prior year provisions",
        "modest release from the 'old years' following a satisfactory 12 months of run off",
        "property catastrophe activity in the form of the Maui fires and yet another torrid period of hail and tornado events in the US Midwest",
        "risk attaching business being affected by the recent Los Angeles wildfires",
        "The year has been impacted by the Floridian Hurricanes Helene and Milton and, without doubt, will suffer to some extent from the recent Los Angeles wildfires, worsening the comparison with previous years",
        "property catastrophe losses around the world showing no signs of abating",
        "The wildfires are a timely reminder of the impact of climate change on lives as well as insured assets",
        "the shadow of 'social inflation' should not be overlooked and we continue to believe the market is still not reacting quickly enough to the likely increase in cost of future jury awards and plaintiffs' demands",
        "This strengthening of the held reserves on the 2022 and prior years of account is largely a result of the changing shape of our loss settlement curves in US casualty business",
        "the practice of litigation funding, whereby insured parties \"sell\" their rights under a policy to a group of investors (often lawyers) who simply try to maximise the claims payments",
        "The increase in provisions in the liability reinsurance class is a result of a revaluation of our historic liability reserves in response to increased levels of litigation funding."
